    "name": "drift-classmix",
    "description": "Task 9.2 drift scenario (vms.loadgen.drift), run against the containerized pipeline with the drift monitor (make demo stack): `python -m vms.loadgen run --scenario bench/scenarios/drift-classmix.yaml`. 4 cameras x 5 FPS for 360 s on four full-length clips (make data; the data-mini clips loop every 10 s, E-050). The monitor's reference is each camera's first 60 s; onsets are at 120 s plus a seeded jitter in [0, 60) s per camera and repetition, recorded in the results (repetitions[].drift.events). Class-mix change: cameras 0 and 2 switch to commons-roncesvalles (a street with cars and cyclists) from their pedestrian scenes; abrupt only (a camera re-pointed, or a feed swapped). Cameras 1 and 3 stay clean. The switch changes the input statistics too: it is a scene change, not a pure class-mix change.\n",
